  "nl_text": "The rschema_0334 database is designed to manage user-generated content, specifically posts and comments, with a focus on user information and relationships between them. The User table stores details about each registered user, including their avatar path, date of birth, email address, first and last names, password, and a unique user ID. The Post table represents individual posts, containing the post content, title, and a foreign key referencing the User table to identify the user who created the post. The Comment table captures comments made on posts, with fields for the comment content, a unique comment ID, and foreign keys referencing both the Post table to identify the post being commented on and the User table to identify the user who made the comment. The User ID in the User table serves as the primary key, while the Post ID in the Post table and the Comment ID in the Comment table also serve as primary keys. The Commented Post ID and Commenter User ID in the Comment table are not nullable, ensuring that every comment is associated with a post and a user, and the Poster User ID in the Post table is also not nullable, indicating that every post must have a creator.",
  "gold_question": "A social media platform's user system is designed as follows:\nThe platform has users. User information includes User ID, First Name, Last Name, Email Address, Avatar Path, Password, and Date of Birth.\nUsers can post posts. Post information includes Post ID, Poster User ID, Post Title, and Post Content.\nUsers can also comment on posts. Comment information includes Commenter User ID, Commented Post ID, and Comment Content.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0334.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0334\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `avatar_path` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `date_of_birth` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `post` (\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `poster_user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`post_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `post_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`poster_user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `comment` (\n  `comment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `commented_post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `commenter_user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`comment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `comment_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`commented_post_id`) REFERENCES `post` (`post_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `comment_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`commenter_user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
